// EXPECT-DIAG: E069
// EXPECT-DIAG: cycle: A_gen1_B -> B -> A_gen1_B
// Regression test: OVH-004 -- a by-value cycle that only exists through a
// CONCRETE generic instantiation must be rejected with StructLayoutCycleError
// (E069), not left to reach Codegen (where it previously segfaulted the
// compiler, exit 139, no output).
//
// `A<T>` alone is not cyclic (its own field is the still-open parameter
// `T`), and `B` alone is not cyclic (its own field is the still-uninstantiated
// generic type `A<B>`) -- the cycle `A<B> -> B -> A<B>` only closes once `T`
// is substituted with the concrete `B`. byValueEdgeTarget() (ResolverCore.cpp)
// used to resolve a `GenericType` field to its TEMPLATE's base name ("A"),
// whose own field is still the placeholder `T` with no further edges, so the
// walk from `B`'s `back: A<B>` field never reached back to the concrete clone
// `A_gen1_B` that the monomorphizer had already put on the same DFS path.
// Fixed by trying the field's mangled instantiation name
// (Monomorphize::instantiatedDeclName()) first.

struct A<T> { val: T }
struct B { back: A<B> }

fn main(): int {
    mut x: A<B> = A::default();
    return 0;
}
